menu "Preset switching"

config MESHTASTIC_PRESET_SETTLE_MS
	int "Radio settle window after a preset switch, in milliseconds"
	default 20
	range 0 1000
	help
	  How long the transmit path waits after a preset switch before keying the
	  PA. The TX path already asks the radio to listen before it talks
	  (LORA_CAD_MODE_LBT), so this is not about politeness — it is about the
	  first CAD after a retune being taken on an AGC that has not settled on
	  the new bandwidth yet, which can read a busy channel as quiet.

	  Costs nothing in steady state: the window is armed by a switch and is
	  already expired by the time the next frame is composed. 0 disables it.

	  docs/MULTI-PRESET-OPERATION.md §4.4, third interlock.

config MESHTASTIC_PRESET_DRAIN_MS
	int "How long a scheduled hop waits for the TX queue to drain"
	default 500
	range 0 30000
	help
	  A frame is composed for the preset the node was on when it was queued —
	  for a default (empty-name) channel the wire channel hash is derived from
	  the preset's display name, so transmitting it after a hop puts the wrong
	  hash on the new preset's frequency. meshtastic_preset_hop() therefore
	  refuses to leave until the outbound queue is empty.

	  This is the bound on that wait. Exceeding it is not an error: the hop is
	  refused, the node stays where it is, and a slot-driven caller simply
	  tries again at the next boundary.

	  docs/MULTI-PRESET-OPERATION.md §4.4, fourth interlock.

endmenu
